From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t31: cap the ALSA period count for the AIC DMA

The IMP frame depth is not the ALSA period count. Using frmNum + 1
periods produced more descriptors than the AIC/PDMA cyclic path can
handle, so the first capture start failed with EINVAL. Use four
periods; the capture chunk still fits in the larger buffer.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/src/t31/openimp_t31_audio.c
+++ b/src/t31/openimp_t31_audio.c
@@ -1029,15 +1029,11 @@
                             const IMPAudioIOAttr *attribute,
                             unsigned int channels)
 {
-    unsigned int periods = attribute->frmNum >= 2 ? attribute->frmNum : 8;
-
-    if (periods > 64)
-        periods = 64;
     memset(config, 0, sizeof(*config));
     config->channels = channels;
     config->rate = attribute->samplerate;
     config->period_size = attribute->numPerFrm ? attribute->numPerFrm : 160;
-    config->period_count = periods + 1;
+    config->period_count = 4;
     config->format = PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE;
     config->start_threshold = config->period_size;
     config->stop_threshold = config->period_size * config->period_count;
